  "body": "The selected-at-base PR1094 k8 provider can save332 primitives per complex\ninvocation in each orientation by scaling one helper coordinate: forward\nL427 enters at1/4, its123 incident ADD coefficients are conjugated, and it exits\nat4. The complete word restores arbitrary helper dirt. Both boundary scales\nare charged, every existing SCALE remains in place, and all non-scalar events\nare unchanged.\n\nThis package proves and checks the exact optimum over477 non-center helpers\nand all integer power-of-two exponents. It uses the strongest retained applicable\nunit/copy-init lowering, including the \u00b11 point discount:149002\u2192148670 forward\nand149018\u2192148686 backward. The original Horner comparator also improves by256.\nFull scalar prefix maxima remain52/68bits under the inherited192-bit local cap.\n\nValidation includes all712 formal data/helper/center input columns, an independent\nliteral predecessor-lowerer replay with893064 primitive steps,8774 integer\ninterval evaluations with outward-tail checks,13 rejection controls and a\nnonconvex unit-discount regression. Original/actualselected archived providers,\nreceipts and lowerer are pinned with a mandatory source inventory. All three\nportable optimized commands are recorded in README.md and VALIDATION.json.\n\nThis is a finite scalar-provider result; native admission, the complete hosted\ninvoice, provider integration and a new assembly/kappa remain open. It claims no\njoint-helper optimum or composition with concurrent stage normalization. Credit\nto the retained icekylinx/Jeremy Kothe/gauge44 supplier lineage, Sagar Thakrar's\ndyadic lowerer, Rohan Arun's PR1094 placement and Douglas Colkitt's source-bound\nreview. @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n",
